# Server & Slurm Rules (READ BEFORE RUNNING ANYTHING HEAVY)

This project runs on a shared university Slurm cluster. See `docs/SERVER_RUNBOOK.md`
and `docs/ENVIRONMENT.md`. Violating these can crash the login node for everyone.

## Golden rule: never compute on the login node

- The login node is for editing, `git`, file inspection, and submitting jobs ONLY.
- NEVER run training, full-dataset preprocessing, or any GPU/heavy-CPU job on the
  login node. Submit via `sbatch`, or use `srun`/`salloc` for an interactive session.
- Quick, cheap, < ~30 s sanity checks (versions, reading one file header, listing
  dirs, building the manifest) are acceptable on the login node.
- A SINGLE-session preprocessing smoke test runs via `srun`, not on the login node.

## Cluster facts (verified)

- Partitions: `gpu2node` (default) and `gpu3node`. Each node: 8 GPUs (`gpu:8`),
  128 CPUs, ~773 GB RAM. TIMELIMIT is effectively unlimited -> ALWAYS set `-t`.
- Modules: `cuda/11.8`, `anaconda3`. Conda env: `mi_torch` (python 3.10).
- KNOWN ISSUE: `mi_torch`'s torch is CPU-only (`torch.version.cuda is None`). GPU jobs
  will not use CUDA until a CUDA-enabled torch is installed (see `docs/ENVIRONMENT.md`).
  Flag this if a GPU run reports `cuda_avail=False`.

## Submitting jobs

- Batch scripts live in `scripts/slurm/*.sbatch`. Run from the project root.
- Logs go to `logs/slurm/%x-%j.out` and `.err` (create `logs/slurm` first).
- Request only what you need (`--gres=gpu:1`, `-c`, `--mem`). Preprocessing is CPU-only
  (no `--gres`).
- Activate inside the job:
  ```bash
  module purge && module load cuda/11.8 anaconda3
  source "$(conda info --base)/etc/profile.d/conda.sh" && conda activate mi_torch
  cd /share/home/yuan/SYX/eeg-mi-online
  ```
- Pass config paths as arguments. Useful: `sbatch`, `squeue -u $USER`, `scancel`,
  `sinfo`, `sacct -j <jobid>`.

## Storage

- Code/configs/manifests/splits/outputs live under the project root.
- Raw dataset (path from `configs/paths.yaml`) is READ-ONLY; never write into it.
- Never write outside `/share/home/yuan/SYX`.

